      "problem": "Find the value of $\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right) \\div \\dfrac{1}{10}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a negative number by a positive number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5} \\div \\dfrac{1}{10} =  \\dfrac {2 \\times 10}{5 \\times 1} = \\dfrac{20}{5} =4,\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right) \\div \\dfrac{1}{10} = -4.\n$$",
